  "result": "Perfect! All 329 tests pass. I've successfully added the mergeCustomers functionality:\n\n**src/customers.js** now includes:\n\n**mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)** function that:\n- Removes the customer with `fromId` from the customers array\n- Reassigns all invoices from `fromId` to `intoId`\n- Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with new arrays (never mutates input)\n- Normalizes both IDs for case-insensitive matching\n- Returns proper error codes for failure cases\n\n**Error handling:**\n- `fail('SAME_CUSTOMER')` if both IDs normalize to the same customer\n- `fail('CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND')` if either customer doesn't exist in the array\n\n**src/errors.js** now includes:\n- `SAME_CUSTOMER` error code with message \"Cannot merge a customer into itself.\"\n\n**test/customers.test.js** has 17 new tests covering:\n- Basic merge: removing fromId customer and keeping intoId\n- Invoice reassignment from one customer to another\n- No mutation of input arrays (verified separately)\n- Error handling: same customer, unknown fromId, unknown intoId, both unknown\n- ID normalization with lowercase, uppercase, spaces\n- Multiple invoices from the same customer\n- Mixed invoices (some from fromId, others from different customers)\n- Preservation of other customers and invoices\n- Verification that returned arrays are new instances\n\nAll 329 tests pass (312 existing + 17 new merge tests).",
